yeah, and that the left side controls are analytical abilities, such as speech, mathematics, things like that. In some sense, we're told that never the twain meet. Now, you've done some research with jazz musicians that has pretty much turned that thinking on its head to make a bad pun. What did you learn from that research about creativity and the two hemispheres of the brain? Okay. So the study that you're talking about was published last year in Neuro Image, also funded by the National Science Foundation. And it was led by David Rosen, who at the time was a graduate student in my lab. And so the topic of the hemispheres of the the brain and creativity is a very controversial topic among psychologists and neuroscientists.

