Thomas Edison and the electric light, for example. And there's some thinking that these insights arise spontaneously, and yet if you look more closely at the lives of some of these people, they've actually spent hundreds of hours working at their craft or their science before they reach these achievements. I'm just wondering how much of genius, as we call it, consists of aha moments and how much is only possible because of the obsessive focus on a particular specialty,

